%% D6 — The three cross-cutting decisions: what it costs, how it fails,
%% and how it defends itself.
%% Show this while narrating cost, resilience and security.

flowchart TB

subgraph COST["💰 COST — where cheap and correct AGREED"]
  direction TB
  K1["1 · LOCAL EMBEDDINGS — bge-m3 on Ollama<br/>ingestion is the HIGH-VOLUME side:<br/>one document = dozens/hundreds of chunks<br/>zero marginal cost AND the teacher's material<br/>never leaves the network. Cost and privacy agreed."]
  K2["2 · EMBEDDING CACHE in Redis, 7d TTL<br/>the same text is never embedded twice"]
  K3["3 · SELF-HOSTED OBSERVABILITY<br/>Prometheus · Loki · Tempo · Grafana ·<br/>Alertmanager · node-exporter · Promtail<br/>the commercial equivalent at this log volume<br/>is a four-figure monthly line<br/>here it is a Compose profile you can not start"]
  K4["4 · OLLAMA LAST IN THE CHAIN — one piece, THREE problems<br/>· no total outage from a vendor failure<br/>· no lock-in: none of the three is irreplaceable<br/>· zero API cost in dev and CI"]
  K5["5 · MINIO INSTEAD OF S3<br/>no per-request cost, no egress cost<br/>API-compatible → migration is an endpoint<br/>and a credential, not a rewritten adapter"]
  K6["6 · THE PLANNER KNOWS IT IS EXPENSIVE<br/>code checks always (free) ·<br/>LLM judge ONLY when flagged or context weak<br/>clean plan = 1 call · worst case 3<br/>judging unconditionally would triple the cost<br/>of the most expensive path for a minority of cases"]
  K7["7 · IT METERS ITSELF — the part most systems skip<br/>provider returns Completion(text, model, TokenUsage),<br/>not a string: the SAME plan costs 0.5¢ or 30¢<br/>depending which model answered, and a string<br/>cannot say which.<br/>UsageLedger sums planner+repair+judge+1/item<br/>across several worker processes.<br/>Budget checked AT THE DOOR, once per plan.<br/>Calendar month UTC: 'it resets on the first' is a<br/>sentence a person can act on."]
end

PAID["…AND WHERE THEY DISAGREED, I PAID<br/><br/>PgBouncer — a container that buys nothing today<br/>Full tracing — containers and complexity<br/>Argon2 — expensive on purpose; I did NOT lower<br/>the cost parameter to get a nicer benchmark<br/><br/>a list of savings without this line<br/>is just a list of corners cut"]

COST === PAID

subgraph RES["🛡️ RESILIENCE — a senior system is one that fails well"]
  direction TB
  R1["CIRCUIT BREAKER, STATE IN REDIS<br/>in-memory → every replica rediscovers the outage<br/>by hammering a dead endpoint, N times<br/>in Redis → the whole FLEET shares one view<br/>a decision that is worthless at 1 replica<br/>and large at 50: made for the system<br/>that does not exist yet"]
  R2["IDEMPOTENCY + task_acks_late — they only work TOGETHER<br/>acks_late alone → duplicated work<br/>idempotency alone → documents lost on every crash<br/>redelivery of PROCESSING/INDEXED is a no-op,<br/>so a worker dying mid-task loses nothing"]
  R3["RETRY 15s → 30s → 60s → FAILED + reason<br/>visible at GET /documents/{id}/status<br/>infinite retry is a clogged queue;<br/>a visible failure is a support team that can answer"]
  R4["NO ORPHANS: the planner runs BEFORE any write<br/>invalid roadmap → 502/503, nothing to clean up<br/>the sequence IS the rollback"]
  R5["PARTIAL is a deliberate state<br/>item 31 failing must not destroy the other 39"]
  R6["GRACEFUL DEGRADATION, MEASURED<br/>100→300 users: latency grows ~linearly,<br/>failures stay at ZERO, container stays healthy"]
  R7["NO POOLED DB CONNECTION HELD DURING AN LLM CALL<br/>a chain can run minutes; holding one would starve<br/>every other route — and the symptom would appear<br/>on endpoints with nothing to do with AI.<br/>You would spend the night in the wrong place."]
end

subgraph SEC["🔒 SECURITY — structure, not a checklist at the end"]
  direction TB
  S1["ARGON2ID · access 15min / refresh 30d<br/>HttpOnly+Secure+SameSite cookies<br/>only the SHA-256 HASH of the refresh is stored<br/>every refresh ROTATES · replaying a revoked one<br/>= REUSE DETECTION → every session killed<br/>(a revoked token in use means it leaked)"]
  S2["NO Bearer header, NO token in localStorage<br/>→ XSS cannot steal the session<br/>→ which is exactly WHY CSRF middleware exists.<br/>You do not get to skip one of the two."]
  S3["OAUTH GOOGLE — state in Redis, single-use<br/>stops login-CSRF (attacker completing the dance<br/>and landing you in THEIR account)<br/>routes registered only when configured:<br/>a disabled feature that still answers on its URL<br/>is one you will forget is disabled"]
  S4["UPLOADS — 3 layers before persisting anything<br/>extension allow-list + declared MIME + MAGIC BYTES<br/>a renamed .exe dies at the third<br/>bounded read → 413, never OOM<br/>stored and parsed, NEVER executed"]
  S5["PROMPT INJECTION — «untrusted_document_context»<br/>every system prompt treats it as DATA<br/>a PDF saying 'ignore previous instructions'<br/>does not get to steer the model"]
  S6["TENANT ISOLATION — the one that would end the product<br/>vector search REFUSES to run unscoped<br/>every repository filters by user_id<br/>routers may not build queries at all"]
  S7["100% ORM, bound parameters<br/>the only raw statement in the project<br/>is SELECT 1 in the readiness probe"]
  S8["API KEYS NEVER IN THE DB — environment only<br/>the DB holds which provider is ENABLED,<br/>not its secret"]
  S9["SUPPLY CHAIN — Dependabot + pip-audit + gitleaks,<br/>the last two BLOCKING<br/>proof in the history:<br/>'fix/upgrade-pypdf-past-two-advisories'"]
  S10["NON-ROOT images · two Docker networks<br/>Postgres, Redis, Ollama, PgBouncer, Tempo:<br/>NOT published to the host<br/>Traefik's unauthenticated :8080 dashboard: OFF"]
  S11["AUDIT — the row is staged INSIDE the caller's<br/>own transaction, right before commit<br/>→ no change without a trail,<br/>no trail without a change<br/>snapshots JSON-safe by construction<br/>(serialization must never break business)<br/>and never copy password_hash"]
end

